
================================================================================================
[A1] sympy: Deser-Levin worldline in the dS4 embedding; Z(s) pullback; KMS periodicity
================================================================================================
  X.X = H**(-2)   (must be 1/H^2)      -> OK
  u.u = -1   (must be -1)         -> OK
  A.A = a**2   (must be a^2: proper acceleration) -> OK
  Z(s) = H^2 X(tau).X(tau-s) = (H**2*cosh(s*sqrt(H**2 + a**2)) + a**2)/(H**2 + a**2)
  Z(s) == (H^2 cosh(kappa s) + a^2)/kappa^2      -> OK
  1 - Z(s) == -2(H^2/kappa^2) sinh^2(kappa s/2)  -> OK
  => hypergeometric argument w = (1+Z)/2 = 1 + beta sinh^2(kappa s/2), beta = H^2/kappa^2:
     the pullback depends on TWO invariants (kappa, beta), not kappa alone.
  KMS geometric periodicity Z(s + 2 pi i/kappa) - Z(s) = 0  -> OK (period 2pi/kappa for EVERY mass)

================================================================================================
[A2] sympy: conformal point reduces to the Deser-Levin kernel; tail coefficient (M^2-2H^2)/8pi
================================================================================================
  Gamma(2)Gamma(1) 2F1(2,1;2;w) = 1/(1 - w)   -> OK
  conformal pullback W(s) = -(H**2 + a**2)/(8*pi**2*(cosh(s*sqrt(H**2 + a**2)) - 1))
  == -kappa^2/(16 pi^2 sinh^2(kappa s/2)) (Deser-Levin thermal kernel, kappa-ONLY) -> OK
  tail coefficient (H^2/8pi)(1/4 - nu^2) = (-2*H**2 + M**2)/(8*pi)  -> OK: (M^2-2H^2)/(8pi), zero IFF M^2 = 2H^2 (conformal)

