[C1] small-mass expansion: T(s) = -(H^2/4pi) + (m^2/8pi)[1 - (2/3) g(y)] + O(m^4)
================================================================================================
  g(y) = y/(2(1-y)) - ln(1-y),  y = -(H^2/kappa^2) sinh^2(kappa s/2)  [xi=0: M=m]
  probe (a,H)=(0.6,0.8), s=1.3:  y = -0.310693,  g(y) = -0.389078
       m       (F-1)/h_-    -> g(y)?           T_exact       T_smallmass     abs.err
    0.20     -0.38527008   -0.389078  -4.8939233678e-02  -4.8925207832e-02    1.40e-05
    0.10     -0.38812783   -0.389078  -5.0429366694e-02  -5.0428488300e-02    8.78e-07
    0.05     -0.38884053   -0.389078  -5.0804363345e-02  -5.0804308417e-02    5.49e-08
  error scaling err(m)/err(m/2) = 15.97, 15.99  (O(m^4) predicts ~16)
  secular regime s >> 1/kappa (still m<<H): g -> -1/2 - kappa s - ln(beta/4):
    T ~ -(H^2/4pi) + (m^2/8pi)[4/3 + (2/3)(kappa s + ln(beta/4))]
    -> the slope offset carries ln(beta) = ln(H^2/kappa^2): EXPLICIT non-kappa structure;
       valid until kappa s ~ 3H^2/m^2, beyond which the exact tail decays as exp(-h_- kappa s).

================================================================================================
[C2] sympy small-s series of the tail SHAPE: trajectory (a^2) enters at s^4
================================================================================================
  2F1(h+,h-;2;y(s)) = 1 + (-M2/8) s^2 + (-M2*(-2*H2 - M2 + 2*a2)/192) s^4 + O(s^6)
  s^2 coefficient = -M^2/8        -> OK (mass-only: NO trajectory info at s^2)
  s^4 coefficient = (M^2/192)(M^2+2H^2-2a^2) -> OK
  => T(s) = (M^2-2H^2)/(8pi) sgn(s) [1 - M^2 s^2/8 + (M^2/192)(M^2+2H^2-2a^2) s^4 + ...]
     STEP   T(0+) = (M^2-2H^2)/8pi = (M^2-2kappa^2+2a^2)/8pi:  d T(0+)/d(a^2) |_kappa = 1/(4pi)
            (exact, mass-independent) -- the LEADING non-kappa structure, at order s^0;
     SHAPE  the a^2 dependence enters at s^4 with coefficient -(M^2/96) a^2 * pref.
     In (kappa, H): s^4 coeff = (M^2/192)(M^2+4H^2-2kappa^2): explicit H^2 at fixed kappa.

